00:01:21,756 --> 00:01:27,656
Okay, so let's get started on lesson number nine, understanding the POC, the point of control.

24
00:01:27,656 --> 00:01:32,156
Point of control, POC, in a bar is often referred to as COT, commitment of traders.

25
00:01:32,656 --> 00:01:36,456
And what it is, it's the price level in a bar where the most volume traded.

26
00:01:36,856 --> 00:01:38,256
And most...

27
00:01:38,756 --> 00:01:40,856
Portafol software will put a box around it.

28
00:01:40,856 --> 00:01:46,456
So as you can see in this chart here where the arrows are pointing, there's a box around.

29
00:01:47,256 --> 00:01:51,056
That's the price level in the bar where the most volume had occurred.

30
00:01:53,508 --> 00:01:55,908
So why is the POC important?

31
00:01:56,008 --> 00:01:58,874
Well, it shows you the exact price in the bar

32
00:01:58,874 --> 00:02:01,740
where volume was heaviest, which is important because this level

33
00:02:01,740 --> 00:02:04,606
can act as support or resistance in the next bar.

34
00:02:05,308 --> 00:02:11,908
You know, imagine knowing where support or resistance will be in the next bar before the next bar starts.

35
00:02:12,408 --> 00:02:14,708
You know, that's quite valuable information.

36
00:02:15,108 --> 00:02:18,908
You know, only an order flows chart will give that information to you.

37
00:02:19,208 --> 00:02:22,571
If you're looking at a normal bar chart, you're not

38
00:02:22,571 --> 00:02:25,934
going to see any information as to, you know, where

39
00:02:25,934 --> 00:02:30,306
in the next bar, you know, price may come down to and react.

40
00:02:32,836 --> 00:02:36,017
So in the point of control, it matters because it

41
00:02:36,017 --> 00:02:39,835
can show you areas where demand has overwhelmed supply or vice versa.

42
00:02:40,536 --> 00:02:46,236
It's going to be the area where the heavy volume was in the bar more often than not.

43
00:02:46,836 --> 00:02:48,768
When point of control occurs in the

44
00:02:48,768 --> 00:02:50,700
middle of the bar, it can be

45
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:53,736
viewed as neutral. As that is where it should normally appear.

46
00:02:54,436 --> 00:02:57,136
In most bars, it's going to appear in the center of the bar.

47
00:02:58,136 --> 00:03:02,336
When point of control occurs near the high or the low, it can often signal a reversal.

48
00:03:03,536 --> 00:03:11,836
It's an area where the heavy volume was in the bar, and why did the market turn around there?

49
00:03:12,336 --> 00:03:18,336
Those are questions you should be asking. Asking of the market when you're analyzing it.

50
00:03:19,236 --> 00:03:21,332
So point of control near the bottom of

51
00:03:21,332 --> 00:03:23,166
the bar indicates that there's usually strong

52
00:03:23,166 --> 00:03:26,834
passive buying, which is often strong enough to turn the market, at least temporarily.

53
00:03:26,836 --> 00:03:28,636
Think of it as stopping volume.

54
00:03:30,036 --> 00:03:31,569
So you can see down here

55
00:03:31,569 --> 00:03:33,102
in this, you know, at the

56
