00:13:43,188 --> 00:13:46,488
It's just acting as your resistance on the way down.

233
00:13:51,332 --> 00:13:55,332
Okay, now, you know, crude is a market. It moves very fast, you know, relative to the five years.

234
00:13:55,432 --> 00:13:57,732
Five years can be a very quiet market

235
00:13:57,732 --> 00:14:00,032
to trade, and it's, you know, sometimes quiet

236
00:14:00,032 --> 00:14:02,332
markets, you know, just don't appeal to people.

237
00:14:02,732 --> 00:14:06,432
You know, people tend to like active markets that are moving fast.

238
00:14:06,432 --> 00:14:10,632
You know, I've said it's your own personal taste, but, you know, the same concepts are applying.

239
00:14:11,632 --> 00:14:13,457
I won't talk about this move up,

240
00:14:13,457 --> 00:14:15,282
but what happens, you have this move

241
00:14:15,282 --> 00:14:18,932
up, and we sort of go sideways, and the market starts to head down.

242
00:14:19,032 --> 00:14:22,932
You've got this selling imbalance, so it's telling you, yeah, the market couldn't continue up.

243
00:14:23,432 --> 00:14:30,532
Now it's starting to sell off. You should be thinking about getting short. And you have this selling imbalance already.

244
00:14:30,932 --> 00:14:32,696
Okay, so you've got the point of

245
00:14:32,696 --> 00:14:34,460
control right here. We came up within

246
00:14:34,460 --> 00:14:37,232
a few ticks of it. And turned around and headed south.

247
00:14:37,232 --> 00:14:42,432
You know, your point of control is here at 3350. We got up to, you know, 47 and turned down.

248
00:14:42,432 --> 00:14:43,635
You know, here your point

249
00:14:43,635 --> 00:14:45,320
of control is at whatever this is,

250
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:48,690
43. Yeah, we got up through it a little bit, and then we continued down.

251
00:14:49,732 --> 00:14:52,832
You know, it's acting as your resistance on the move down.

252
00:14:55,196 --> 00:14:59,596
That's an example in crude, which is a much faster moving market than five years.

253
00:15:00,096 --> 00:15:01,841
Again, here's a crude chart again.

254
00:15:01,841 --> 00:15:03,586
We're moving up, and point of

255
00:15:03,586 --> 00:15:06,495
control is acting as your support on the move up.

256
00:15:07,496 --> 00:15:12,696
You have this change here in supply and demand, and now on the way down,

257
00:15:14,296 --> 00:15:16,596
your point of control is acting as resistance.

258
00:15:16,996 --> 00:15:21,196
You know, you're getting through it by, you know, two ticks, three ticks, which is fine.

259
00:15:22,096 --> 00:15:23,543
You know, when you're trying

260
00:15:23,543 --> 00:15:24,990
to, you know, get short

261
00:15:24,990 --> 00:15:27,016
on a pullback or get long on

262
00:15:27,016 --> 00:15:28,463
a pullback, sometimes the market

263
00:15:28,463 --> 00:15:33,094
overshoots it by, you know, a couple of ticks, you know, three ticks, sometimes four ticks.

264
00:15:33,096 --> 00:15:35,596
I mean... That's just the nature of the market.

265
00:15:35,796 --> 00:15:38,796
It doesn't always turn right at the level that you want it to.

266
00:15:39,096 --> 00:15:40,496
In the best of all worlds, yes.

267
00:15:41,296 --> 00:15:44,596
But the problem, sometimes it doesn't give you that chance.

268
00:15:45,996 --> 00:15:52,696
You miss your entry and the market just continues in the direction that it should be headed.

269
00:15:54,496 --> 00:15:57,196
Okay, now let's look at an E-mini chart.

270
00:15:58,296 --> 00:15:58,996
It's the same thing.

271
00:15:58,996 --> 00:15:59,996
Here's your point of control.

272
00:16:00,096 --> 00:16:01,896
You're assuming the market's going to move down.

273
00:16:02,096 --> 00:16:04,796
You've got your point of control right here. We're staying below it.

274
00:16:04,896 --> 00:16:08,196
You know, you come right back up to the point of control in the next bar and sell off.

275
00:16:09,596 --> 00:16:14,796
Now you've got the single print right at that point of control. It's telling you, hey, there's no more follow-through.

276
00:16:15,896 --> 00:16:17,173
Now you're at the point of

277
00:16:17,173 --> 00:16:18,450
control on this bar. You get

278
00:16:18,450 --> 00:16:22,495
up within a tick of it. You just get past of it by a tick, rather, and sell off.

279
00:16:23,296 --> 00:16:24,196
Controls right here.

280
00:16:24,696 --> 00:16:27,796
Get up to within, you know, one tick and sell off.

281
00:16:27,896 --> 00:16:31,296
You know, here again, we get up to within one tick and are going lower.

282
00:16:32,596 --> 00:16:33,449
You know, it's

283
00:16:33,449 --> 00:16:34,872
something you can, you know,

284
00:16:34,872 --> 00:16:36,295
trade around or, you know,

285
00:16:36,295 --> 00:16:37,718
place your stop around, you

286
00:16:37,718 --> 00:16:39,994
know, if you like to trail your stop.

287
00:16:42,496 --> 00:16:50,296
Okay, again, this is a Euro stock. It's a stock index. And you get up to this level.

288
00:16:50,396 --> 00:16:51,660
You've got a single

289
00:16:51,660 --> 00:16:52,924
print, single print, a

290
00:16:52,924 --> 00:16:54,820
ratio. Bounce low here with some

291
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:58,296
stopping volume. It's a weak one, but it's stopping volume nevertheless.

292
00:16:58,296 --> 00:16:59,296
It's giving you a ratio.

293
00:16:59,996 --> 00:17:02,396
But you've got three ratios.

294
00:17:04,596 --> 00:17:09,996
Telling you, hey, the market isn't getting the follow-through that you're expecting, so look to get short.

295
00:17:10,996 --> 00:17:18,296
And if you're looking to get short, you're using the point of controls as going to be your resistance levels.

296
00:17:18,596 --> 00:17:20,843
So if you're not short in this bar,

297
00:17:20,843 --> 00:17:22,528
looking to get short in this

298
00:17:22,528 --> 00:17:24,494
bar, it comes up within a tick.

299
00:17:24,496 --> 00:17:26,096
Here it comes up back within a tick.

300
00:17:26,096 --> 00:17:27,396
Here it comes up within a tick.

301
00:17:27,496 --> 00:17:29,196
Here it comes right back to a tick.

302
00:17:30,896 --> 00:17:33,896
So you have chances to get short in there.

303
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:40,020
Okay, you know, just real quick, here's the bond chart.

304
00:17:40,020 --> 00:17:42,620
You know, same thing, you know, on the way up and on the way down.

305
00:17:43,620 --> 00:17:45,420
You know, we're working our way up, working our way up.

306
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:49,120
You know, you've got the buying imbalances. It's not really meeting much resistance.

307
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:50,076
And you get up

308
00:17:50,076 --> 00:17:51,510
here. And, you know, what happens

309
00:17:51,510 --> 00:17:52,705
is you get a buying

310
00:17:52,705 --> 00:17:54,618
imbalance here, a selling imbalance, a selling imbalance.

311
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:59,220
And right at the bar, you're seeing a shift in supply and demand happen right up here at the high.

312
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:00,945
You know, you get

313
00:18:00,945 --> 00:18:02,182
the early buying imbalance, then, you

314
00:18:02,182 --> 00:18:03,419
know, late in the bar, you

315
00:18:03,419 --> 00:18:04,244
get, you know, selling

316
00:18:04,244 --> 00:18:06,719
in there, you get a big negative delta right at the high.

317
00:18:06,820 --> 00:18:10,320
It's telling you, hey, the market's, you know, primed to start to sell off.

318
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:11,102
Okay, so, you know,

319
00:18:11,102 --> 00:18:12,275
you want to get in and,

320
00:18:12,275 --> 00:18:13,448
you know, where are you going

321
00:18:13,448 --> 00:18:14,817
to be looking to place your stop?

322
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:17,920
You know, if you're getting in, you know, early in the next bar,

323
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:21,507
You're going to have a stop up here

324
00:18:21,507 --> 00:18:23,494
at the point of control, and you're going

325
00:18:23,494 --> 00:18:27,219
to be looking at the point of control as your resistance on the move down.

326
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:29,581
If you want to trail your stop, you

327
00:18:29,581 --> 00:18:31,127
can trail your stop around the

328
00:18:31,127 --> 00:18:34,219
point of controls. The market is staying below the point of controls.

329
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:37,581
In this case, the market dropped pretty quick,

330
00:18:37,581 --> 00:18:39,352
and there really wasn't any much

331
00:18:39,352 --> 00:18:41,418
retracement back into the point of controls.

332
00:18:45,136 --> 00:18:47,836
And, you know, lastly, this is, again, this is a bond chart.

333
00:18:51,336 --> 00:18:54,336
Early on, it really looked like we're going sideways.

334
00:18:54,636 --> 00:18:56,812
You get a red bar, a green bar,

335
00:18:56,812 --> 00:18:58,444
a red bar, a green bar,

336
00:18:58,444 --> 00:19:01,436
and you're getting the point of controls around the same levels.

337
00:19:01,536 --> 00:19:03,036
You've got three in a row here.

338
00:19:04,136 --> 00:19:06,317
Even to a lesser extent, you draw it

339
00:19:06,317 --> 00:19:07,953
out here, you've got point of

340
00:19:07,953 --> 00:19:10,134
control, point of control at the same level.

341
00:19:10,436 --> 00:19:11,536
Here, it's a little bit higher.

342
00:19:13,836 --> 00:19:15,036
It's tricky when it's like this.

343
00:19:15,236 --> 00:19:17,494
It's in a range because you want to

344
00:19:17,494 --> 00:19:19,752
take it as support, especially when you're seeing

345
00:19:19,752 --> 00:19:24,834
you're all just spending a lot of time above it, but you can go below it pretty quick.

346
00:19:26,336 --> 00:19:33,136
This is a case where your support can also become your resistance if you break the support level.

347
00:19:33,936 --> 00:19:36,536
When it's strung out like this, I find that

348
00:19:37,936 --> 00:19:42,148
oftentimes when it breaks through in the opposite direction, like

349
00:19:42,148 --> 00:19:46,360
here I'm inclined to think it's a support level because

350
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:51,835
you have the imbalances here early and we're sort of holding it later.

351
00:19:53,136 --> 00:19:57,056
I don't remember what the rest of this chart looked like, we

352
00:19:57,056 --> 00:20:02,936
rallied or sold off, but I tend to find when we're spending more time above the support level,

353
00:20:04,036 --> 00:20:09,236
that if we start to come out of it and sell off, it's going to become resistance very fast.

354
00:20:09,436 --> 00:20:13,136
And oftentimes I find once it starts to sell off, can sell off pretty quick.

355
00:20:16,036 --> 00:20:18,736
Okay, so that's the end of Lesson 9, Pointing Controls.

356
00:20:18,736 --> 00:20:22,936
In the next lesson, I will explain the importance of delta and how to interpret it.

357
00:20:23,336 --> 00:20:27,086
Delta is something that's extremely unique to order flows that

358
00:20:27,086 --> 00:20:30,086
you're not going to find on normal charts,

359
00:20:30,086 --> 00:20:32,336
normal bar charts, normal candlestick charts.

360
00:20:32,836 --> 00:20:36,763
And it's very powerful, especially if you can

361
00:20:36,763 --> 00:20:40,690
sort of mesh it in with a couple

362
00:20:40,690 --> 00:20:43,635
other analysis, like point of controls.

363
00:20:45,936 --> 00:20:53,436
It's something that once you understand delta, it's going to really make your trading much better and more powerful.

364
00:20:54,436 --> 00:20:55,736
So that's the end of Lesson 9.

